content.text:
### Result
- [Screenshot of viewport](screenshots/mobile-battle-3.png)
### Ran Playwright code
```js
// Screenshot viewport and save it as screenshots/mobile-battle-3.png
await page.screenshot({
  path: 'screenshots/mobile-battle-3.png',
  scale: 'css',
  type: 'png'
});
```

The arena mark numeral is not visible at all! Why? It might be behind the .backdrop? No. It's probably because `-webkit-text-stroke` with transparent color at opacity .12 over dark is too subtle, or the mark is positioned above and clipped by the arena overflow? `.arena` has no overflow hidden. The mark is at top:-2%, font 112px; should appear around y=90-200. I see nothing. Maybe the color `transparent` with `-webkit-text-stroke` works only if `-webkit-text-fill-color`? It worked for title outline. The mark might be behind the `.arena::before`? z-index 0; fighters z1. The screenshot shows a subtle vertical line from the mark? At top center there's a vertical line at x=195 from y=60-130: that's probably the arena-mid::before? No, mid is at 400. Wait, there's a vertical line at top center around y=55-130. That might be the `arena-mark`? No text. Could be the `.arena-mid::before` with top -18% bottom -18% and z-index -1; because mid is static and full width? Hmm.

Actually the line at top center might be the arena mark's border/stroke? No.

Look at the huge ring circle: starts at y~115 and spans to 650. The mark numeral should be at top center. Not visible. Maybe the `strong` is inherited `text-transform`? No. Color transparent + stroke 0.12 is extremely subtle; on a dark background, 12% gold should be barely visible but perceptible. Here not.

The vertical line at top center is likely `.arena-mid::before`: mid is at y~400 but its pseudo extends -18% of mid height (mid height ~40) = -7px only, so no. Hmm, maybe the line is the mark's `strong` glyph "I" (Roman numeral I) rendered as a vertical stroke! Yes! The numeral is "I", so at 112px it's a single vertical bar, and with 12% gold it's the line at top center. That's why it looks like a line. It actually fills the top area subtly. But it could be mistaken for a glitch. For rings with "IV", "VII" etc. it will show. For I, a vertical line. Maybe fine—it's a Roman numeral watermark. But it's very subtle and looks like a stray line. Increase opacity/stroke to .18 and add a horizontal top/bottom serif? Roman numeral I in a serif font has serifs; at 112px it should show serifs. The line seems ~60px tall. Could be.

I think the mark should be more visible but not intrusive: stroke .18, font-size 150px on mobile. The top gap still large but now has a subtle numeral. Maybe add the boss's name faint? Hmm.

The mobile layout still has large top/bottom empty bands. The top band now has the faint I. The bottom band is empty. Could add a bottom caption "THE FIRST FLAME" or the boss passive? The passive is under enemy status. The player statuses at bottom.

Maybe reduce mobile arena height by moving the command deck up and adding a footer below? No.

Alternatively, make the enemy card fill the top by aligning its content larger: portrait 140, name 18, intent bigger, HP. The player card can be larger too. This would reduce empty space. Let's increase mobile enemy portrait to 140 (grid col 140), player 72. Increase font sizes: enemy name 16, intent body 11, player name 15, HP. That adds ~40px. The top gap still ~150.

Could put a decorative "gods" line at top with the boss intro quote in the empty top area after intro. E.g., move the battle log to the top (order 0) and style the first line (narrator intro) big? The log currently at y=410 under the turn. If we move turn + log to the top (order 0) with the intro quote, the top gap above becomes content. But flex center redistributes. Yet if we set the arena to `justify-content:space-between` with the content height including top log, it might fit. Let's estimate content: mid 40 + enemy 250 + player 90 = 380. Container 668. Free 288. With space-between, gaps 144 each; top/bottom padding 8. Top: mid at 60, enemy at 240, player at 610? Player 90 ends 700, deck at 720. Actually order mid(0), enemy(1), player(2): mid 60-100, gap 144, enemy 244-494, gap 144, player 638-728 → overlaps deck at 720 by 8. With slightly smaller cards, fine. This would fill vertical space with distance and put the turn/log at the top, making a nice "chronicle at top, god in the middle, you at the bottom" layout. But if the log has 2 lines, mid 45. Could fit.
However when statuses/passive add height, player could overflow. Flex items can shrink? The portrait is fixed, text can wrap. Risk.

Alternatively use `justify-content:space-between` and set `.arena { overflow:hidden }` to avoid deck overlap; player might get cut. Not good.

Maybe set explicit mobile grid rows:
```
.arena {
 display:grid;
 grid-template-rows: auto 1fr auto;
 grid-template-areas: "enemy" "mid" "player";
}
```
with enemy at top, mid center, player at bottom. Grid 1fr middle absorbs extra space, pushing enemy top and player bottom. That's exactly space-between but safe: the middle row expands. Then:
- enemy in row1 at top, player row3 at bottom, mid centered in remaining space.
- The empty space between enemy and mid and mid and player is distributed inside the 1fr row (mid centered), which may look intentional: a chasm between gods and you, with the log floating in between.
- No overlap; if content exceeds, rows min-content and the 1fr shrinks to 0.
This is better than flex center. Let's use:
```
.arena { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr; grid-template-rows:auto minmax(30px,1fr) auto; grid-template-areas:"enemy" "mid" "player"; align-items:stretch; }
.fighter-enemy{grid-area:enemy; align-self:start}
.arena-mid{grid-area:mid; align-self:center}
.fighter-player{grid-area:player; align-self:end}
```
The arena has padding top 6 bottom 2. Enemy at top y=58. Player at bottom y~620. Mid at center ~400. That fills the whole area and gives a dramatic gap. Yes! This is the right layout.

But the command deck at 720; player bottom 720. Good. The player card 90 tall at y=620-716. The enemy card 240 from y=58-298. Mid centered around 400. Gaps 100 and 100. That's intentional spacing, not empty top. 

Add a floor glow under the player maybe. The big ring behind ties it.

Let's implement grid mobile. Remove flex properties. In `.arena` mobile:
```
display:grid;
grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr);
grid-template-rows: auto minmax(24px, 1fr) auto;
grid-template-areas: "enemy" "mid" "player";
align-items: stretch;
gap: 0;
padding: 8px 0 4px;
```
- `.fighter-enemy { grid-area: enemy; order: unset; align-self:start; }`
- `.arena-mid { grid-area: mid; align-self:center; position:static; ... }`
- `.fighter-player { grid-area: player; align-self:end; }`
- `.fighter { width:100% }` already.

This should look great. Let's patch. Also remove order.

